[h1]False Flag Detector[/h1]

Pirates and smugglers often fly under someone else's flag: a Scale Plate trader entering Teladi space shows up as a Teladi ship, and nothing on the map tells you otherwise. This extension adds two research projects that let your sensor network spot them.

[h2][b]Features[/b][/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]False Flag Detection[/b] research: any ship flying under a false flag that one of your ships, stations or satellites can see is reported, with its name, ID, sector and the flag it shows.
[*] [b]True Owner Identification[/b] research: a more expensive follow-up; every report also names the true owner of the ship.
[*] [b]Context menu[/b]: right-click a detected ship to see a [b]False flag[/b] line; with True Owner Identification researched, the true owner is shown beside it in its faction colour. Hover over it for the full report.
[*] [b]Notifications[/b]: a warning in the ticker and an entry in the logbook's Alerts, each can be switched off. For 10 minutes after the report the logbook entry shows the ship on the map; a ship carrying a Shadow Tracker keeps that button.
[*] [b]Shadow Tracker[/b]: with [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3676424693]Shadow Tracker[/url] installed and the option on, a Shadow Tracker device is attached to every detected ship while you have free devices in your inventory.
[/list]
[h2][b]Limitations[/b][/h2]
[list]
[*] A ship is reported once per disguise: again when it switches to another false flag, or drops its flag and later takes one again. A ship that leaves your sensor coverage and comes back under the same flag is reported again only when [b]Report again after being out of view for[/b] is set.
[*] Detection only names the ship. To expose it in the game, scan it as usual: a finished scan strips the false flag, and the local forces can respond.
[*] Your own ships flying under a cover faction are never reported.
[/list]
