[h2][b]Installation[/b][/h2]

You can download the latest version via Steam client - [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3820999285]False Flag Detector[/url]
Or you can do it via the Nexus Mods - [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/x4foundations/mods/2462]False Flag Detector[/url]

[h2][b]Save state[/b][/h2]

[b]No[/b] (removing the extension does not break saves).

[h2][b]Usage[/b][/h2]

Research [b]False Flag Detection[/b] at your headquarters. From then on the detector checks every few seconds which ships under a false flag are seen by any of your assets, and reports the new ones. Research [b]True Owner Identification[/b] afterwards to see who really owns them.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-FalseFlagDetector/refs/heads/main/docs/images/research_detection.png[/img]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-FalseFlagDetector/refs/heads/main/docs/images/research_identification.png[/img]

Each detected ship is reported in the message ticker:

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-FalseFlagDetector/refs/heads/main/docs/images/ticker.png[/img]

and in the Alerts section of the logbook, with a button to show the ship on the map. The button disappears 10 minutes after the report, so an old entry does not keep revealing where the ship is now; it stays for a ship that carries a Shadow Tracker:

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-FalseFlagDetector/refs/heads/main/docs/images/logbook.png[/img]

While a detected ship is in view or carries a Shadow Tracker, its context menu carries a [b]False flag[/b] line with the true owner beside it; hover over the line for the full report:

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-FalseFlagDetector/refs/heads/main/docs/images/context_menu.png[/img]

[h2][b]Options[/b][/h2]

An options page is available via the [b]Extension Options[/b] menu:

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-FalseFlagDetector/refs/heads/main/docs/images/options.png[/img]
[list]
[*] [b]Show a notification in the message ticker[/b] - on by default.
[*] [b]Write an entry to the logbook[/b] - on by default.
[*] [b]Scan interval[/b] - how often the detector checks, from 3 to 60 seconds - 5 by default.
[*] [b]Ships reported per scan[/b] - at most this many new ships are reported by one scan; the others wait for the next scans, so a sensor network that suddenly sees many disguised ships does not flood the logbook. 0 reports all of them at once - 3 by default.
[*] [b]Report again after being out of view for[/b] - a ship that comes back into view under the same false flag after at least this many minutes out of view is reported again, from 0 to 120 minutes; 0 never reports it again - 0 by default.
[*] [b]Attach a Shadow Tracker to every detected ship[/b] - off by default; available only with Shadow Tracker 8.00.04 or newer, which lets other extensions request tracking.
[*] [b]Debug Level[/b] - None, Debug or Trace; writes detailed lines to the game log.
[/list]
